# Curated artefact -- Phase 3b, M1b run R2: QNX 8.0.0 as the hypervisor host at EL2 (VHE) on all six Cortex-A78AE cores of the Jetson Orin Nano (2026-09-10).
# Image m1b-p6: startup-t234-orin-nano -vvv -P6 -Q enable,el2-host -m992M -Wkeep -Dtcu, kimg sha256 prefix 85970fe84cb5ed644e2cced6,
# entered by kexec from L4T R36.4.7. PART 1 was captured live over J14 (TCU, UART2_TXD pin 4), FT232R adapter, 115200 8N1, from
# Linux's kexec line to the first firmware lines after the reset. PART 2 is /sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0 read on the next boot.
# RESULT: every M1b pass criterion held in this run, and run R2b repeated it with the identical image. The library printed
# 'Enabling EL2 host hypervisor support (VHE)'. After its own hypervisor_init every core printed HCR_EL2=0000030488000000 (E2H and
# TGE set) and ran the board's INTID 28 probe with nothing enabled or unmasked:
#   - arming the EL2 physical timer (INTID 26, the positive control) raised pending bit 26;
#   - arming the EL2 virtual timer raised bit 28, and masking it cleared it;
#   - verdict=wired on cores 0-5.
# The syspage carries qtime intr:28 and hypinfo flags 1, and all six cores parked in smp_spin. procnto and user space ran at EL2, and
# smpcheck printed 'census hyp qtime_intr=28 hypinfo_flags=0x1', 'census tick=ok ms=100', 'SMPCHECK CENSUS PASS' and
# 'SMPCHECK RESULT PASS cpus=6/6 secs=60 reasons=none'. The image then warm-reset the board itself (PMC reset reason MAINSWRST), and
# L4T answered again 148 s after the launch.
# OBSERVED, NOT A CRITERION:
#   - The five secondaries entered at EL2 with the same firmware register values as M2's CPU_ONs, which were issued from EL1.
#   - The two cluster-1 cores ran smpcheck's busy loop at 57.1 million iterations/s, against about 400 million on cluster 0. That is
#     the same fixed rate they had under -Q disable.
# NOT SHOWN: qvm, a guest, stage-2 translation or any hypervisor workload (that is M3); INTID 28 outside the Non-secure view; which PPI
# served each secondary's kernel timer; any timing figure; repeatability beyond R2 and R2b.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

